Error [E0152]: A `String` is not a `Regex` pattern
  --> tests/ui/regex_bare_string.jet:5:19
    |
  5 |     print(re.find("\\d+", "id=42") ?? "none")
    |                   ^^^^^^
 Why: Regex patterns are typed literals, so Jet can validate them before the program runs
 Fix: Write `.{"..."}` here, or call `re.compile(text)` for a pattern built at run time
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0152
